      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t this always the same as `pkvm_get_loaded_hyp_vcpu()`?\n\nIn fact, this function is a little odd as it means we have three different VM identifiers:\n\n (1) `pkvm_get_loaded_hyp_vcpu()` \u003d\u003e the currently loaded vCPU\n (2) The `vm_handle`\n (3) The `kvm_cpu_context`\n \nFurthermore, `kvm_guest_ffa_handler()` actually takes the vCPU as an argument, so we\u0027re probably better off propagating that instead of going via the handle.\n\nIn other words:\n\n```\nstatic struct kvm_ffa_buffers *ffa_get_buffers(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu)\n{\t\n\tif (!hyp_vcpu)\n\t\treturn \u0026host_buffers;\n\n\treturn \u0026pkvm_hyp_vcpu_to_hyp_vm(hyp_vcpu)-\u003effa_buf;\n}\n```",
